# Keep modules short

Prefer a module that does one job and stays easy to read. When a file you are editing is over **800 lines**, or your change would push it over, consider splitting it along the responsibilities it already has.

A major refactor — moving most of the file, renaming the public surface, or breaking one module into several — needs a yes first. Say what you would split and where, then wait. Do not start that move in the same turn.

A small extraction can land with the change that made the file too long: one helper, one type, or one already-separate concern, with callers updated. Do not restructure neighboring modules to get under the line.

```text
# BAD — recommender.py is 900 lines and you silently split it into
# five modules and rewrite the imports

# GOOD — "recommend.py is over 800 lines. Split stream/finish into
# stream.py and leave packing here?"
# Wait. On a yes, do that split.
```
